<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 1,751,371 tonnes of oilseed in May 1997 against 1,538,407 tonnes in May 1996, the Agriculture Secretariat said.</p>
<p>(Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean	     1,120,252    (881,957)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 555,967    (576,470)</p>
<p> Linseed		     396	(5,910)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	   6,729	(4,433)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	     68,007     (69,637)</p>
<p>Output in May was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     198,061    (162,495)    894,636     (726,238)</p>
<p> Sunflower   219,159    (234,162)    229,182     (234,023)</p>
<p> Linseed	   114	(2,965)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut     3,322	(1,704)	4,800	   (nil)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   10,766     (10,591)     32,715	(32,379)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    4,749   (5,251)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower  2,223     (nil)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed	281   (3,864)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to May, with the same period</p>
<p>in 1996 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean	     3,137,573    (3,072,782)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed     2,530,755    (2,487,922)</p>
<p> Linseed		  38,741	 (82,629)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  62,137	 (33,093)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	    165,095	(162,379)</p>
<p>Output in January through May (1996 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     559,958    (597,704)  2,505,141  (2,507,436)</p>
<p> Sunflower 1,000,273    (984,039)  1,073,680  (1,052,099)</p>
<p> Linseed	12,102     (25,285)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    24,115     (21,293)     35,668     (20,872)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   26,282     (24,879)     79,542     (74,998</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    16,644 (16,518)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower   5,079  (5,166)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    26,127 (53,068)</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
